ll satisfied after removal), then add to removed list. Check required symbols: after removing this node, does each required symbol appear at least once among retained nodes? Since we only remove one node at a time (and its children already removed), we can precompute a symbol count map for retained nodes (initially all nodes). As we remove nodes, decrement counts for that node's symbol. Before removing, check if any required symbol would become zero after decrement. Also we need to consider that when we remove a node, we also remove its children? But children are already removed, so counts already decreased. So we just check for this node's symbol.\n\nImplementation details:\n\n- Input case is a dict with keys: nodes (list of dicts each with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility), required_symbols (list of strings), _case_nonce (ignore).\n- Parse nodes into dict: node = {id: {...}}\n- children_map: for each node, collect list of child ids.\n- root_id: find node with parent null.\n- Determine processing order: sort nodes by (-depth, id) so deeper first, then alphabetically by id.\n- Initialize removed_set = set()\n- Initialize symbol_counts: dict mapping symbol to count of nodes not removed (initially count all nodes). Since nodes have symbol, we can count.\n- For each node in order:\n   if not node['removable']: continue\n   if node['id'] == root_id: continue\n   # check children all removed\n   children = children_map.get(node['id'], [])\n   if any(child_id not in removed_set for child_id in children):\n      continue\n   # check required symbols if we remove this node\n   sym = node['symbol']\n   # if this node's symbol is required and its count in current retained is exactly 1, then removing would make 0.\n   if sym in required_symbols_set:\n       if symbol_counts[sym] == 1:\n           continue\n   # okay to remove\n   removed_set.add(node['id'])\n   symbol_counts[sym] -= 1\n   # record removal order\n   removed_order.append(node['id'])\n\n- After loop,